{"title":"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a real-valued <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> <i>very convex</i> if\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e298e1ba811b64c1726bdb5ffab3dddb4f284e0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {f(x) + f(y)}{2} \\ge f\\left(\\frac {x + y}{2}\\right) + |x - y|\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>holds for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Prove that no very convex function exists.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13f250f1481908fb7f400238ab1c0c2b04d8c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\ge x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/98706f7aa2f6bea45bbb982073a57d09968deb3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x, 2b = y-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />. Then a function is very convex if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adbb4e5a67cb7e5cd72326c5a1a619f3650ab5de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(a) + f(a+2b)}{2} \\ge f(a + b) + 2b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"264\" height=\"40\" />, or rearranging,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/3/6a36f41315521af133a2e6d89575640cccf81ad2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left[\\frac{f(a+2b)-f(a+b)}{b}\\right]-\\left[\\frac{f(a+b)-f(a)}{b}\\right] \\ge 4\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/5/085b3b6ba45a2f37ed3651d0f0682df722c611fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a) = \\frac{f(a+b) - f(a)}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"181\" height=\"38\" />, which is the slope of the secant between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/00977373c17ef7a6e70c369e33e6b9f10e6ec399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,f(a))(a+b,f(a+b))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be arbitrarily small; then it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140a39f00e2d66c1393ae5e36bb50676b2971922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a+b) - g(a) &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18f2a7263fc48c992600c2b9731235f69438fb3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a+2b) - g(a+b) &gt; 4,\\, \\cdots, g(a+kb) - g(a+ [k-1]b) &gt; 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"480\" height=\"18\" />. Summing these inequalities yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/8/85817b13cc745280fd60aaa9f48cba7ab106ea57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(a+kb)-g(a) &gt; 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/53230126f99a9b450081f84587fd05f1c4f4a812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\rightarrow \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> (but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e397d87c7b395efd5eee5a2345a738b8b882b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt;&lt; \\frac{1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"58\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e373a3b4e95c691182675a88adb702469e9c828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bk &lt; \\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> is still arbitrarily small), we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00814725b306151e6e1de1ba2f623f5dbd25ca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{k \\rightarrow \\infty} g(a+kb) - g(a) = g(a + \\epsilon) - g(a) &gt; \\lim_{k \\rightarrow \\infty} 4k = \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"429\" height=\"25\" />. This implies that in the vicinity of any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the function becomes vertical, which contradicts the definition of a function. Hence no very convex function exists.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose, for the sake of contradiction, that there exists a very convex function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is convex if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a39f08fb9ec75a006906cb7bf0e63bae4673f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> is convex, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a constant. Thus, we may set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c59bd9d20bcc9cd7fea79dd1f88c8d6332ce55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> for convenience.\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e6d32292b985067370bad2ed403a215fa25d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfcfd1983607a40a604499a0bffed4e6afa441a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-1) = B.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> By the very convex condition,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe81548506e6fc4eca7a40ed2026ba37bb46016.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(0) + f\\left(2^{-n}\\right)}{2} \\ge f\\left(2^{-(n+1)}\\right) + \\frac{1}{2^n}.\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"38\" />\nA straightforward induction shows that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/8/1e85d6678d6c56e85f60417c61e644cb64dabdcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(2^{-n}\\right) \\le \\frac{A - 2n}{2^n}\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"37\" />\nfor all nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\nUsing a similar line of reasoning as above,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86ca5e851710d7fda339ef1889086bf7b043a0b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(-2^{-n}\\right) \\le \\frac{B - 2n}{2^n}.\\]\" width=\"161\" height=\"37\" />\nTherefore, for every nonnegative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cd7a1ed4af4348b784133280fde9d94120917b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(2^{-n}\\right) + f\\left(-2^{-n}\\right) \\le \\frac{A+B-4n}{2^n}.\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"37\" />\nNow, we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> large enough such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/5/f55f7cc9655f213205261b486431411d82aabeef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; \\frac{A+B}{4} - 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"38\" /> This is always possible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are fixed for any particular function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> It follows that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8db41701559e800fc945e2dd2314eb9c7e02a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(2^{-n}\\right) + f\\left(-2^{-n}\\right) &lt; \\frac{1}{2^{n-2}}.\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"37\" />\nHowever, by the very convex condition,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f88ac610104a2f840cd3a25dcb26ae6761aed3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(2^{-n}\\right) + f\\left(-2^{-n}\\right) \\ge \\frac{1}{2^{n-2}}.\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"37\" />\nThis is a contradiction. It follows that no very convex function exists.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define the symmetric average\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/3/f2375d1e6c295ec1f8417f08c3b3cd409c677602.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F(x, y) = \\frac{f(x) + f(y)}{2}.\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"38\" />\nThen the inequality becomes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bbf756d2dc10bdb430aa01638a279b94e2ea038.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F(x, y) \\ge f\\left( \\frac{x + y}{2} \\right) + |x - y|.\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c0a86663edb0dccee099a47d48b1b19a4ee6cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x - y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> is not differentiable along the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e33fa7c7b2ce1a18e6e0a6d3ef6c08bd1958722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, the surface defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/d/b5dc8f2a060280ac0742748be613d4f9ae9aca76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> must have a permanent kink along the diagonal. A kink is a sharp crease where the surface fails to have a well-defined tangent plane.\n</p><p>If f were a true function on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> satisfying the inequality at all scales, then this kink would have to persist no matter how closely x and y are chosen. That means the graph of F never becomes smooth near the diagonal.\n</p><p>But every differentiable real-valued function f produces a smooth symmetric average F. Therefore, the presence of a permanent kink contradicts the assumption that f is differentiable at any scale. The kink cannot be removed by local smoothing.\n</p><p>Hence, the geometric shape of the inequality forces a kink that no function f can produce, so no function can be very convex.\n</p><p>~Lopkiloinm\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume, for contradiction, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7006aed57e3aa9c0755ed9c2e88e8be56f8f103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db184aa513ee499bebc8ae3e917b48da56fcf86b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(x)+f(y)}{2}\\geq f\\!\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)+|x-y| \\qquad \\text{for all } x,y\\in\\mathbb{R}.\\]\" width=\"424\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2d7d87f936c9a3f571f66bf8af5b5a36145748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a-h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31c824e916a36843fab1135929d32f0d4f92bec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a+h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e7ad6b53ca0e132dfc8ac1759106b9c8c47b7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(a+h)+f(a-h)-2f(a)\\geq 4|h| \\qquad \\text{for all } a,h\\in\\mathbb{R}.\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/5064bf054fb82ac871e34f32e3ee04cf4b29d249.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta_h^2 f(a):=f(a+h)+f(a-h)-2f(a)\\geq 0 \\qquad \\text{for all } a,h\\in\\mathbb{R},\\]\" width=\"492\" height=\"20\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is convex. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/48700d698a2b3e7e78d99fa1ccc28b5000dd1ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu=f&#39;&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" /> in the distributional sense. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> is a nonnegative locally finite Borel measure.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf642186044923923da160295ed941ca3913bdc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />, the second difference can be written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/8/0f86cc9eea33710157ec7995b8b55e8bb8fcdbe6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta_h^2 f(a)=\\int_{\\mathbb{R}} 2(h-|x-a|)_+\\,d\\mu(x),\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"40\" />\nwhere\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69c000bd958f95b4a7fd6fd14c0ca98b546e62d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(t)_+=\\max\\{t,0\\}.\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebd2d56667f2b6e299096af7838f10703d64e46d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(h-|x-a|)_+\\leq h\\,\\mathbf{1}_{[a-h,a+h]}(x),\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"19\" />\nwe get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e673cc832bf39676ee173614f44432a1db1bb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta_h^2 f(a)\\leq 2h\\,\\mu([a-h,a+h]).\\]\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>On the other hand, the hypothesis gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cfc8324307dbcd9fc5956202468a03a83790c55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Delta_h^2 f(a)\\geq 4h.\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />\nHence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5141349fb341c25628aa1a1131edcade01a8b1bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mu([a-h,a+h])\\geq 2 \\qquad \\text{for every } h&gt;0.\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/e/9de83f6e6df5ac14a361f56362f968739509df71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h\\downarrow 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />, continuity from above yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/f/f0f4f6d9a7c80de953e56f0884d21c875dc7044a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\mu(\\{a\\})\\geq 2.\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> was arbitrary, every point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906fddead65545297c74bbc2ca83cd01f3f9ecc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> is an atom of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" /> of mass at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, contradicting local finiteness of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8c833ed800824727cd7bd2fb9de1a12ad7e674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mu$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore no function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7006aed57e3aa9c0755ed9c2e88e8be56f8f103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db184aa513ee499bebc8ae3e917b48da56fcf86b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(x)+f(y)}{2}\\geq f\\!\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)+|x-y| \\qquad \\text{for all } x,y\\in\\mathbb{R}.\\]\" width=\"424\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/17101fec0d4ba5dc2dc01015b7024edc85151786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=a-h, y=a+h,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d4007e5f4a484add36dd73eae84b8ebbd1a4856f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,h&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. For a <i>very convex</i> function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, it follows that\n\\begin{equation}\nf(a+h)+f(a-h)-2f(a)\\ge 4h\\tag{1}\n\\end{equation}\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8389ac57ec348e456fa0a14c6a2f49ad4c46c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{h}(t)=f(t+h)-f(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"20\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/203f15da7494e4c76599ad5080c6fc9f73bea23c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_{h}(a)\\ge D_{h}(a-h)+4h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"195\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Consider a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de3257800f85cb71ed4ab112cd0441f872f90300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=\\frac{1}{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081c26c49779dd5efff56dbe40e0bd4e431e27f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\in\\{0,1,\\ldots, N-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />, we define\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f74e17b03b9c508c7704f31792fb0e38c6cb02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_{k}=f((k+1)h)-f(kh)\\]\" width=\"204\" height=\"18\" />\nWe get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb8a9d260695a9038575c24bc1c48f6f10d0855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_k\\ge D_0+4kh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" /> by the above inequality. Hence\n\\begin{align*}\nf(1)-f(0)&amp;=\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}D_k\\\\\n&amp;\\ge \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}D_0+4kh\\\\\n&amp;=ND_0+2(N-1)\n\\end{align*}\nOr <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5bad0f5121abe81b53ff9b44686624fa1ff0d23a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D_0\\le -2+\\frac{f(1)-f(0)+2}{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"220\" height=\"40\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7feafaad547221b78da2fb819a6b796d25051ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(h)-f(0)=D_0\\le -2+\\frac{f(1)-f(0)+2}{N}\\quad (2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"40\" />. \n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89340b7c8b24bb3f0c1fb1b36d324fb02e29b7d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=f(-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" /> satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed1b8f2dbed5bd256ee495a0a34071270a5718a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{g(x)+g(y)}{2}=\\frac{f(-x)+f(-y)}{2}\\ge f\\left(\\frac{(-x)+(-y)}{2}\\right)+\\lvert x-y\\rvert =g\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)+\\lvert x-y\\rvert,\\]\" width=\"636\" height=\"43\" />\nwhich means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is <i>very convex</i> too. \nWe obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/7266444fb09fa0cd7005dd3e3a35f00281c47314.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-h)-f(0)\\le -2+\\frac{f(-1)-f(0)+2}{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"317\" height=\"40\" />. Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> yields\n\\begin{align*}\nf(h)+f(-h)-2f(0)\\le -4+\\frac{f(1)+f(-1)-2f(0)+4}{N}\\tag{3}\n\\end{align*}\nHowever, by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, the given property of a <i>very convex</i> function,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16413cffc749e2f973f642d625f6f3a8a283e71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(h)+f(-h)-2f(0)\\ge 4h=\\frac{4}{N}\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"37\" />\nAlong with the upper bound of the same expression obtained from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d574cacabc490b19f67e6ed06671e5604fa400.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=f(1)+f(-1)-2f(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"210\" height=\"20\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ff6af89c9c961ba65e863e7f691157279ebc909.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4}{N}\\le -4+\\frac{4+C}{N}\\iff\\frac{C}{N}\\ge 4\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"37\" />\nIn this regard, having an arbitrarily large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />-value results in a contradiction. Hence, no such <i>very convex</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> exists, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO\" title=\"2000 USAMO\">2000 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194343\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 523/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1284/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17826/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.942      1 -tot